  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>, such that the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is _____ ."
  },
